  "notes": "pc-r008: Compute-starve sweep \u2014 n_recursions in {1,2,4,8} (inner latent-recursion depth per outer supervision step). arm='absolute', seed=42, data_seed=42 held fixed (the pc-r007 absolute/s42 config; R=8 is the pc-r007 anchor). SINGLE variable = n_recursions. Motivation: pc-r007 solved K=4 at 100% with the 4-hop answer appearing in y by outer step 1, but each outer step runs n_recursions=8 inner z-updates (~16 inner transformer applications by step 1) \u2014 ample compute to compute all 4 hops within one/two outer steps rather than one hop per outer step (front-loading). NOTE: n_cycles is inert (stored but never read by TinyRecursiveModel.forward); the true recurrence-depth knob is n_recursions. This corrects pc-r007 finding 7, which mis-attributed the per-step inner compute to n_cycles=3. Test: hold n_supervision=8 and shrink n_recursions. Genuine iteration (outer loop as a hop clock) => the correct K=4 answer still emerges, at a possibly-later outer step; front-loaded shallow compute => final K=4 acc degrades and/or emergence slides past the available steps as R drops. Everything else identical to pc-r007 (bf16, every-step probe, concat encoder, 100k train, dim=256, n_supervision=8). Questions: (1) At which outer step does y first reach 1.0 as R shrinks? (2) Does z_probe_acc still saturate the composition chain under starved compute? (3) Does final K=4 acc hold at R in {1,2,4}?",
